Let the top-left square have side $a$. The small square (side 1) sits to its right, at the bottom of its height, so:

- the square above the small one has side $a - 1$;
- the bottom-left square has side $a + 1$ (it spans the top-left square and the small one);
- the big right square starts at the top of the small square and ends at the bottom of the bottom-left square, so its side is $a + (a + 1) - (a - 1) = a + 2$.

The big square begins $a + 1$ from the left edge, so its right edge is at $(a + 1) + (a + 2) = 2a + 3$. The top square ends at $a + (a - 1) = 2a - 1$. Hence $h = (2a + 3) - (2a - 1) = 4$.

**Answer: (C) 4**
